body:
The hasNextPage logic is overly simplistic and may produce incorrect results. It only checks if `fetchedCount === pageSize`, which will incorrectly show "has next page" when the total count happens to be an exact multiple of pageSize.

For example, if there are exactly 100 records with pageSize=20, after fetching all 5 pages (0-19, 20-39, ... 80-99), the last page will have 20 items, so hasNextPage will be true, but there's actually no next page.

Consider using the `count` field from PaginatedResult to accurately determine if there are more pages:
```
const totalFetched = pages.reduce((sum, p) => sum + p.value.length, 0) + result.value.length;
const hasMore = result.count > totalFetched;
```
```suggestion
      const totalFetched = skip + result.value.length;
      const hasMore =
        typeof (result as any).count === 'number'
          ? (result as any).count > totalFetched
          : result.value.length === pageSize;
```
